{"event_type":"review","id":"4372178a50b60e0731f34aa7072d10f8e5824e3446a110275587f3c49f5a9d53","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T20:51:44Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dc76d94b5b9d3e70e03140c9f0a233f07bd7a0da44c6c3f82455ebd60ce051ff","sha256":"dc76d94b5b9d3e70e03140c9f0a233f07bd7a0da44c6c3f82455ebd60ce051ff"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d7ac021659c739524abd6b6b61dfa69f7241884b3078767a65704e84ffeafbff","sha256":"d7ac021659c739524abd6b6b61dfa69f7241884b3078767a65704e84ffeafbff"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/25ca57faa1b472ac5d581df2ec95e5601a16e63decd635462984126daf4d15f2","sha256":"25ca57faa1b472ac5d581df2ec95e5601a16e63decd635462984126daf4d15f2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/39114a2030ab9a6ffe15d7f043103c6f832b6b61abd5ce8060f386b0985c654f","sha256":"39114a2030ab9a6ffe15d7f043103c6f832b6b61abd5ce8060f386b0985c654f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2797b57ee315f3122cbe39dd4586066c74bf074c6b1c50c9ee6ab2bb7f8ad84d","sha256":"2797b57ee315f3122cbe39dd4586066c74bf074c6b1c50c9ee6ab2bb7f8ad84d"}],"attempt_id":"9f6df88b138ab1e491fcaa70edca60354e5b0c9d04f721ecb35bc5c643afad8e:0:1","base":"7c5d1077c25f050eb03e9554aaa009797a6458d4","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b1d1b9db9161a1696a507ef3e7a1a01a1003e9c8","body":"**Ensure the image before writing the env file.**\n\n`src/sandbox/backend.ts:348` writes `child.env` before `image inspect` and `pull` run. The comment at `src/sandbox/backend.ts:324-326` says the file \"exists only while `create` reads it\". With this change, the scrubbed env file stays on disk for the whole pull, which can last up to `CONTAINER_PULL_TIMEOUT_MS` (300 s). That env includes passthrough values. The pull does not need the env file. Run `inspect` and `pull` first, then write the file just before `create`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         let created: SandboxLaunchResult;\n         try {\n-          const envFile = join(envDir, 'child.env');\n-          await writeFile(envFile, envFileText, { mode: 0o600 });\n-          const createArgs = containerArgv(\n-            resolved,\n-            request.workspace,\n-            request.network,\n-            envFile,\n-            request.argv,\n-          ).slice(3); // omit `<cli> run --rm`\n           const inspected = await runChild(\n             launcher,\n             ['image', 'inspect', resolved.image],\n             controlOptions,\n           );\n           const pulled = inspected.ok\n             ? inspected\n             : await runChild(launcher, ['pull', resolved.image], {\n                 ...controlOptions,\n                 timeoutMs: CONTAINER_PULL_TIMEOUT_MS,\n               });\n-          created = pulled.ok\n-            ? await runChild(\n-                launcher,\n-                ['create', '--pull', 'never', '--name', name, ...createArgs],\n-                controlOptions,\n-              )\n-            : pulled;\n+          if (pulled.ok) {\n+            const envFile = join(envDir, 'child.env');\n+            await writeFile(envFile, envFileText, { mode: 0o600 });\n+            const createArgs = containerArgv(\n+              resolved,\n+              request.workspace,\n+              request.network,\n+              envFile,\n+              request.argv,\n+            ).slice(3); // omit `<cli> run --rm`\n+            created = await runChild(\n+              launcher,\n+              ['create', '--pull', 'never', '--name', name, ...createArgs],\n+              controlOptions,\n+            );\n+          } else {\n+            created = pulled;\n+          }\n         } finally {\n```\n</details>","id":"018e65683f55c23d865f650deb55c581d3d83f82474c2cb4331040dd75baa368","intervals":[],"path":"src/sandbox/backend.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Ensure the image before writing the env file."}],"head":"24428a9a51ccdfa6ee6b9c4d87920f011894b08d","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"1bb872a71e2e41435004337032f7f3310e5d74d3","intervals":[[1,1257]],"path":"experimental/sandbox-host/probe.ts"},{"blob":"5917903930b2075e0f8bb74c803a7257ffbcffe6","intervals":[[1,135]],"path":"experimental/sandbox-host/sandbox-certify.mjs"},{"blob":"b1d1b9db9161a1696a507ef3e7a1a01a1003e9c8","intervals":[[1,3],[5,5],[7,14],[16,17],[196,204],[356,362],[364,364],[367,379]],"path":"src/sandbox/backend.ts"},{"blob":"de5fb94d487cb460b60472d6e2c85d8adf3a16c7","intervals":[[1,321]],"path":"src/sandbox/launcher.ts"}],"job_id":"9f6df88b138ab1e491fcaa70edca60354e5b0c9d04f721ecb35bc5c643afad8e:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"9809e3325ea85428adea85b6720b63e934582d33","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/sandbox/backend.ts"},"merge":"6476299ea7a0334014f85267206b14ebb0542ba4","method":"pre-merge","pre":"31cf2ce10422f077674b2a70da66a89638176251","source_path":"src/sandbox/backend.ts"},"blob":"b1d1b9db9161a1696a507ef3e7a1a01a1003e9c8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/sandbox/backend.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"6476299ea7a0334014f85267206b14ebb0542ba4","method":"pre-merge","pre":"31cf2ce10422f077674b2a70da66a89638176251","source_path":"src/sandbox/launcher.ts"},"blob":"de5fb94d487cb460b60472d6e2c85d8adf3a16c7","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/sandbox/launcher.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"6476299ea7a0334014f85267206b14ebb0542ba4","method":"pre-merge","pre":"31cf2ce10422f077674b2a70da66a89638176251","source_path":"experimental/sandbox-host/probe.ts"},"blob":"1bb872a71e2e41435004337032f7f3310e5d74d3","disposition":"included","mode